Each square of the three by three grid is painted so that the whole picture has at least the two lines of symmetry indicated. Each grid square is painted one solid color. What is the maximum number of colors that could have been used? [asy]size(100);
draw((0,0)--(0,3)--(3,3)--(3,0)--cycle);
draw((1,0)--(1,3));
draw((2,0)--(2,3));
draw((0,1)--(3,1));
draw((0,2)--(3,2));
draw((-0.2,-0.2)--(3.2,3.2),dashed);
dot((0,0));dot((3,3)); dot((1.5,0)); dot((1.5,3));
draw((1.5,-0.3)--(1.5,3.3), dashed);
[/asy]

final_text:
The probability that both get the same number is the sum of the probabilities that both get 1, both get 2, both get 3, or both get 4:

\[
\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^2+\left(\frac{2}{10}\right)^2+\left(\frac{3}{10}\right)^2+\left(\frac{4}{10}\right)^2
\]

\[
= \frac{1}{100}+\frac{4}{100}+\frac{9}{100}+\frac{16}{100}
= \frac{30}{100}
= \frac{3}{10}
\]

The answer is \(\boxed{\frac{3}{10}}\).

