Compute the dot products:
\[
\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}=
\begin{pmatrix}2\\3\\-1\end{pmatrix}
\cdot
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-1\\0\end{pmatrix}
=2(2)+3(-1)+(-1)(0)=4-3=1
\]
\[
\mathbf{w}\cdot \mathbf{w}=
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-1\\0\end{pmatrix}
\cdot
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-1\\0\end{pmatrix}
=2^2+(-1)^2+0^2=5
\]
Thus,
\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v}
=\frac{\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w}\cdot \mathbf{w}}\mathbf{w}
=\frac{1}{5}
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-1\\0\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac{2}{5}\\[2pt]
-\frac{1}{5}\\[2pt]
0
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{5} \\ -\frac{1}{5} \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\).

\[
\frac{\csc \theta}{\sin \theta}-\frac{\cot \theta}{\tan \theta}
\]

Use identities:
\[
\csc \theta=\frac{1}{\sin \theta},\qquad \cot \theta=\frac{\cos \theta}{\sin \theta},\qquad \tan \theta=\frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta}
\]

First term:
\[
\frac{\csc \theta}{\sin \theta}
=\frac{1/\sin \theta}{\sin \theta}
=\frac{1}{\sin^2 \theta}
\]

Second term:
\[
\frac{\cot \theta}{\tan \theta}
=\frac{\cos \theta/\sin \theta}{\sin \theta/\cos \theta}
=\frac{\cos^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta}
\]

So,
\[
\frac{1}{\sin^2 \theta}-\frac{\cos^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta}
=\frac{1-\cos^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta}
=\frac{\sin^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta}
=1
\]

The answer is \(\boxed{1}\).

